Introducing the **Nanofiber Drag Net**. This is a physical web of electrospun polymer nanofibers, each acting as a tiny, independent filter element. The network’s architecture is a non-woven mat with varying fiber diameters and densities. Instead of processing data, the system uses the aerodynamic resistance of air passing through the web. When a high-velocity gas stream is applied, the fibers align and trap particles based on their size and velocity.
